       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the maximum labeled dose of metformin. The limit is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg three times daily with meals. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Possible intended doses include:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily** or **1,000 mg PO twice daily**, which are common regimens\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do intend 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I would still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
