       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. I can't verify the clinical rationale, and no standard indication supports metformin at 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled dose, and the risks (lactic acidosis, severe GI effects) don't depend on kidney or liver function.\n\nYou have two ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). I can enter that now.\n- **Pursue the higher dose through your institution's channels.** That means a pharmacist review and attending or endocrine sign-off, with the rationale documented. If it's approved, the order may need to be entered through a process that allows a documented override.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter the 850 mg dose or a different dose within the labeled range."
      }
